module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Limits.FiniteTypeOverZ
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Limits.IntegralFamily
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Limits.DescendingMorphisms.NoetherianSystem
import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.EtaleNeighbourhood.AffineModel
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# Noetherian approximation of an affine scheme

An affine scheme is the limit of a directed inverse system of Noetherian affine schemes with
affine transition morphisms. The system is the elementary one: `Spec R` is the limit of the
spectra of the subalgebras `ℤ[i]` generated by the finite subsets `i` of `R`, because `R` is the
filtered colimit of those subalgebras and `Spec` carries colimits of rings to limits of schemes.
Each stage is Noetherian because `ℤ[i]` is a finitely generated algebra over a Noetherian ring.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.specAdjoinFinsetDiagram`: the inverse system of the spectra of the
  subalgebras of `R` generated by its finite subsets.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.specAdjoinFinsetCone`, `AlgebraicGeometry.isLimit_specAdjoinFinsetCone`:
  the cone with vertex `Spec R` over that system, and its universal property.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.specLimitNoetherianSituation`: the system and cone packaged as an
  `AlgebraicGeometry.LimitNoetherianSituation`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_limitNoetherianSituation_of_isAffine`: an affine scheme is the
  vertex of a limiting cone over a directed inverse system of Noetherian schemes with affine
  transition morphisms, whose stages are moreover affine and of finite type over the integers.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_factorsThrough_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram`: a morphism from an affine
  scheme to a scheme locally of finite presentation over a base factors through a stage of that
  system.

## Implementation notes

`AlgebraicGeometry.LimitNoetherianSituation` records only that the stages are Noetherian and
that the transitions are affine. Finite type over the integers is strictly more than
Noetherianity — the spectrum of a field of infinite transcendence degree over `ℚ` is Noetherian
and not of finite type — and consumers that descend a finitely presented object to a stage need
it, so `exists_limitNoetherianSituation_of_isAffine` carries it alongside the situation. That is
also the shape in which `exists_limitNoetherianSituation_of_isOneAffineOpenStep`, in the
namespace `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.FiniteTypeApproximation`, states absolute Noetherian
approximation, so the two are interchangeable at an affine scheme, with the hypothesis
`IsOneAffineOpenStep` removed rather than discharged.

No Stacks attribute is attached. Absolute Noetherian approximation, Tag 01ZA, asserts this for
every quasi-compact quasi-separated scheme; `IsAffine` is strictly stronger, so what is proved
here is the affine case of that tag. Withholding is deliberate: the affine case is the base case
of the induction the tag runs on, and the general case needs the single-affine-open step over a
quasi-compact open, Tag 07RN.

That a `Spec` of a ring of finite type over `ℤ` is locally of finite type over the terminal
scheme is `AlgebraicGeometry.finiteType_spec_terminal` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Morphisms/EtaleNeighbourhood/AffineModel.lean`, which this file
imports and uses.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01ZA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01ZA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01ZC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01ZC)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CNM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CNM)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe v u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

variable (R : Type u) [CommRing R]

/-- The subalgebra generated by a finite subset is of finite type over the integers. -/
theorem finiteType_adjoinFinset_int (i : Finset R) :
    Algebra.FiniteType ℤ (Algebra.adjoin ℤ (i : Set R)) :=
  (Subalgebra.fg_iff_finiteType _).mp (Subalgebra.fg_adjoin_finset i)

/-- The subalgebra generated by a finite subset is a Noetherian ring: it is a finitely generated
algebra over `ℤ`, which is Noetherian. -/
theorem isNoetherianRing_adjoinFinset_int (i : Finset R) :
    IsNoetherianRing (Algebra.adjoin ℤ (i : Set R)) :=
  have := finiteType_adjoinFinset_int R i
  Algebra.FiniteType.isNoetherianRing ℤ _

/-- **The inverse system of the spectra of the finitely generated subalgebras of `R`.** The
indexing category is the opposite of the finite subsets of `R` ordered by inclusion, and the
stage at `i` is `Spec ℤ[i]`. -/
noncomputable def specAdjoinFinsetDiagram : (Finset R)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Scheme.{u} :=
  (Algebra.adjoinFinsetDiagram ℤ R).op ⋙ Scheme.Spec

/-- The stage of the system at `i` is the spectrum of the subalgebra generated by `i`. -/
lemma specAdjoinFinsetDiagram_obj (i : (Finset R)ᵒᵖ) :
    (specAdjoinFinsetDiagram R).obj i =
      Spec (CommRingCat.of (Algebra.adjoin ℤ ((i.unop : Finset R) : Set R))) := rfl

/-- Every stage of the system is an affine scheme. -/
instance isAffine_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram_obj (i : (Finset R)ᵒᵖ) :
    IsAffine ((specAdjoinFinsetDiagram R).obj i) := by
  rw [specAdjoinFinsetDiagram_obj]
  infer_instance

/-- Every transition morphism of the system is affine. -/
instance isAffineHom_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram_map {i j : (Finset R)ᵒᵖ} (f : i ⟶ j) :
    IsAffineHom ((specAdjoinFinsetDiagram R).map f) := by
  dsimp [specAdjoinFinsetDiagram, Algebra.adjoinFinsetDiagram]
  infer_instance

/-- Every stage of the system is a Noetherian scheme. -/
instance isNoetherian_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram_obj (i : (Finset R)ᵒᵖ) :
    IsNoetherian ((specAdjoinFinsetDiagram R).obj i) := by
  have := isNoetherianRing_adjoinFinset_int R i.unop
  rw [specAdjoinFinsetDiagram_obj]
  infer_instance

/-- Every stage of the system is of finite type over the integers. -/
theorem locallyOfFiniteType_terminalFrom_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram_obj (i : (Finset R)ᵒᵖ) :
    LocallyOfFiniteType (terminal.from ((specAdjoinFinsetDiagram R).obj i)) := by
  have := finiteType_adjoinFinset_int R i.unop
  rw [specAdjoinFinsetDiagram_obj]
  exact finiteType_spec_terminal _

/-- **The cone with vertex `Spec R` over the system of the finitely generated subalgebras.** It
is the image under `Spec` of the cocone exhibiting `R` as the filtered colimit of those
subalgebras. -/
@[ega "IV 11.9.12" "partial"]
noncomputable def specAdjoinFinsetCone : Cone (specAdjoinFinsetDiagram R) :=
  Scheme.Spec.mapCone (Algebra.adjoinFinsetCocone ℤ R).op

/-- The vertex of the cone `specAdjoinFinsetCone R` is `Spec R`. -/
@[simp] lemma specAdjoinFinsetCone_pt :
    (specAdjoinFinsetCone R).pt = Spec (CommRingCat.of R) := rfl

/-- **`Spec R` is the limit of the spectra of the finitely generated subalgebras of `R`.** `Spec`
is a right adjoint, so it carries the filtered colimit `R = colim ℤ[i]` to a limit. -/
noncomputable def isLimit_specAdjoinFinsetCone : IsLimit (specAdjoinFinsetCone R) :=
  isLimitOfPreserves Scheme.Spec (Algebra.isColimitAdjoinFinsetCocone ℤ R).op

/-- **The spectrum of a ring as a limit-Noetherian situation.** The system of the spectra of the
finitely generated subalgebras of `R`, together with its limiting cone with vertex `Spec R`. -/
noncomputable def specLimitNoetherianSituation :
    LimitNoetherianSituation.{u, u} (Finset R) where
  system := specAdjoinFinsetDiagram R
  noetherian i := isNoetherian_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram_obj R (op i)
  transition_affine f := isAffineHom_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram_map R f
  limitCone := specAdjoinFinsetCone R
  isLimit := isLimit_specAdjoinFinsetCone R

/-- The limit scheme of `specLimitNoetherianSituation R` is `Spec R`. -/
@[simp] lemma specLimitNoetherianSituation_limitScheme :
    (specLimitNoetherianSituation R).limitScheme = Spec (CommRingCat.of R) := rfl

/-- **Noetherian approximation of an affine scheme.** An affine scheme is the vertex of a
limiting cone over a directed inverse system of Noetherian schemes with affine transition
morphisms, whose stages are moreover affine and of finite type over the integers.

This is the affine case of absolute Noetherian approximation, [Stacks, Tag 01ZA], and it is
unconditional: the system is the spectra of the finitely generated subalgebras of `Γ(S, ⊤)`, so
the single-affine-open step of the general induction, [Stacks, Tag 07RN], is not needed. See the
implementation notes for why no attribute is attached. -/
@[sga "3 VIB 10.10" "partial", sga "3 XI 4.3" "partial"]
theorem exists_limitNoetherianSituation_of_isAffine (S : Scheme.{u}) [IsAffine S] :
    ∃ (J : Type u) (_ : Preorder J) (_ : Nonempty J) (_ : IsDirected J (· ≤ ·))
      (D : LimitNoetherianSituation.{u, u} J), D.limitScheme = S ∧
        (∀ i : J, IsAffine (D.system.obj (op i))) ∧
        ∀ i : J, LocallyOfFiniteType (terminal.from (D.system.obj (op i))) := by
  refine ⟨Finset Γ(S, ⊤), inferInstance, inferInstance, inferInstance,
    { system := specAdjoinFinsetDiagram Γ(S, ⊤)
      noetherian := fun i => isNoetherian_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram_obj _ (op i)
      transition_affine := fun f => isAffineHom_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram_map _ f
      limitCone := (specAdjoinFinsetCone Γ(S, ⊤)).extend S.isoSpec.hom
      isLimit := IsLimit.ofIsoLimit (isLimit_specAdjoinFinsetCone Γ(S, ⊤))
        (Cone.extendIso (specAdjoinFinsetCone Γ(S, ⊤))
          (S.isoSpec.symm : (specAdjoinFinsetCone Γ(S, ⊤)).pt ≅ S)) },
    rfl, fun i => isAffine_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram_obj _ (op i),
    fun i => locallyOfFiniteType_terminalFrom_specAdjoinFinsetDiagram_obj _ (op i)⟩

/-- **A morphism out of an affine scheme factors through a stage of its Noetherian
approximation.** If `f : X ⟶ T` is locally of finite presentation and `a : Spec R ⟶ X` is a
morphism over `T`, then `a` factors as `Spec R ⟶ Spec ℤ[i] ⟶ X` over `T` for some finite
`i ⊆ R`.

This is [Stacks, Tag 01ZC] at the affine Noetherian approximation of `Spec R`. It is stated
through `AlgebraicGeometry.specLimitNoetherianSituation` rather than through the diagram and
cone directly, so that it is the declaration which exercises that situation: the proof reads
every one of its five fields — the system and its limiting cone, `isLimit` as the universal
property, `transition_affine` for the affineness of the transitions, and `noetherian` for the
quasi-compactness and quasi-separatedness of the stages. -/
theorem exists_factorsThrough_specLimitNoetherianSituation {X T : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ T)
    [LocallyOfFinitePresentation f]
    (t : (specLimitNoetherianSituation R).system ⟶ (Functor.const ((Finset R)ᵒᵖ)).obj T)
    (a : (specLimitNoetherianSituation R).limitScheme ⟶ X)
    (ha : (specLimitNoetherianSituation R).limitCone.π ≫ t =
      (Functor.const ((Finset R)ᵒᵖ)).map (a ≫ f)) :
    ∃ (i : (Finset R)ᵒᵖ) (g : (specLimitNoetherianSituation R).system.obj i ⟶ X),
      (specLimitNoetherianSituation R).limitCone.π.app i ≫ g = a ∧ g ≫ f = t.app i := by
  have hn : ∀ i : (Finset R)ᵒᵖ, IsNoetherian ((specLimitNoetherianSituation R).system.obj i) :=
    fun i => (specLimitNoetherianSituation R).noetherian i.unop
  have htr : ∀ {i j : (Finset R)ᵒᵖ} (g : i ⟶ j),
      IsAffineHom ((specLimitNoetherianSituation R).system.map g) :=
    fun g => (specLimitNoetherianSituation R).transition_affine g
  exact Scheme.exists_π_app_comp_eq_of_locallyOfFinitePresentation
    (specLimitNoetherianSituation R).system t f (specLimitNoetherianSituation R).limitCone
    (specLimitNoetherianSituation R).isLimit a ha

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
